 ### Supersampling Baseline
-A baseline method for evaluating NeRF on multiscale data by training on full-resolution images and using brute-force supersampling during evaluation, or training on multiscale data with supersampling during both training and evaluation [S23]. For every pixel, multiple jittered rays are sampled uniformly at random through the spatial footprint of the pixel. The mean of the rendered values is used as the predicted color in the loss function [S23]. This baseline relies on 'oracle' scale information that does not exist for most datasets [S23]. Performance-wise, the 16x supersampling baseline performs worse than mip-NeRF and is significantly more expensive during both training and evaluation [S23].
